  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/010212">Definition <span data-tag="010212">5.1.6.2</span>.</a>compact object!completelycompletely compact Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category which admits small colimits. We will say that an object $C \in \calC $ is <em>completely compact</em> if the functor $j_{C}: \calC \rightarrow \widehat{\SSet }$ corepresented by $C$ preserves small colimits. </p>
